WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:00.440
All right.

00:00.480 --> 00:00.720
Great.

00:00.720 --> 00:02.400
So with that we have a data model.

00:02.400 --> 00:05.160
And we can say we have something called a data products.

00:05.160 --> 00:08.920
And we will be sharing this data products with different types of users.

00:08.920 --> 00:12.720
And there is something that's every data products absolutely needs.

00:12.760 --> 00:14.840
And that is that data catalog.

00:14.840 --> 00:20.640
It is a document that can describe everything about your data model, the columns, the tables, maybe

00:20.640 --> 00:22.640
the relationship between the tables as well.

00:22.680 --> 00:27.320
And with that, you make your data products clear for everyone and it can be for them, way easier to

00:27.360 --> 00:31.000
derive more insights and reports from your data products.

00:31.000 --> 00:32.680
And what is the most important one?

00:32.880 --> 00:36.280
It is time saving because if you don't do that, what's going to happen?

00:36.280 --> 00:41.880
Each consumer, each user of your data products will keep asking you the same questions about what do

00:41.880 --> 00:42.800
you mean with this column?

00:42.800 --> 00:43.760
What is this table?

00:43.800 --> 00:48.920
How to connect the table A with the table B, and you will keep repeating yourself and explaining stuff.

00:48.920 --> 00:54.320
So instead of that you prepare a data catalog, a data model, and you deliver everything together to

00:54.360 --> 00:55.000
the users.

00:55.000 --> 00:57.720
And with that you are saving a lot of time and stress.

00:57.760 --> 01:02.560
I know it is annoying to create a data catalog, but it is investments and best practices.

01:02.560 --> 01:04.120
So now let's go and create one.

01:04.160 --> 01:09.160
Okay, so now in order to do that, I have created a new file called Data Catalog in the folder documents.

01:09.160 --> 01:11.040
And here what we're going to do is very straightforward.

01:11.040 --> 01:14.160
We're going to make a section for each table in the gold layer.

01:14.160 --> 01:17.160
So for example we have here the table dimension customers.

01:17.160 --> 01:19.730
What you have to do first is to describe this table.

01:19.730 --> 01:24.890
So we are saying it stores details about the customers with the demographics and geographics data.

01:24.890 --> 01:27.330
So you give a short description for the table.

01:27.330 --> 01:31.570
And then after that you're going to go and list all your columns inside this table and maybe as well

01:31.570 --> 01:32.330
the data type.

01:32.330 --> 01:35.770
But what is very important is the description for each column.

01:35.770 --> 01:40.330
So you give a very short description like for example here the gender of the customer.

01:40.330 --> 01:45.530
And now one of the best practices of describing a column is to give examples, because you can understand

01:45.570 --> 01:48.770
quickly the purpose of the columns by just seeing an example.

01:48.810 --> 01:49.090
Right.

01:49.090 --> 01:53.250
So here we are seeing we can find inside it a male female and not available.

01:53.250 --> 01:56.250
So with that the consumer of your table can immediately understand aha.

01:56.290 --> 02:01.890
It will not be an M or an F, it's going to be a full friendly value without having them to go and query

02:01.890 --> 02:02.930
the content of the table.

02:02.930 --> 02:05.650
They can understand quickly the purpose of that column.

02:05.650 --> 02:10.210
So with that, we have a full description for all the columns of our dimension, the same thing we're

02:10.210 --> 02:11.930
going to do for the products.

02:11.930 --> 02:17.130
So again a description for the table and as well a description for each column and the same thing for

02:17.130 --> 02:17.890
the facts.

02:17.890 --> 02:18.650
So that's it.

02:18.650 --> 02:22.610
With that you have like a data catalog for your data products at the code layer.

02:22.610 --> 02:28.170
And with that the business user or the data analyst have better and clear understanding of the content

02:28.170 --> 02:29.130
of your gold layer.

02:29.170 --> 02:30.010
All right, my friends.

02:30.010 --> 02:31.730
So that's all for the data catalog.

02:31.770 --> 02:37.170
In the next step we're going to go back to drool where we're going to finalize the data flow diagram.

02:37.170 --> 02:37.970
So let's go.
